====================================================================================
THE LEAST-EIGENVALUE CERTIFICATE for the LRC apex floor (mac-mini-S37)
====================================================================================

[1] CERTIFICATE -- the doublet Gram 2I + A(C_p) is POSITIVE DEFINITE iff p is ODD:
      p parity  lambda_min A(C_p)  lambda_min 2I+A  C_p bipartite?      cert
      3   odd           -1.00000          1.00000              no     PSD>0
      5   odd           -1.61803          0.38197              no     PSD>0
      7   odd           -1.80194          0.19806              no     PSD>0
     11   odd           -1.91899          0.08101              no     PSD>0
     13   odd           -1.94188          0.05812              no     PSD>0
      4  even           -2.00000          0.00000             YES  SINGULAR
      6  even           -2.00000          0.00000             YES  SINGULAR
    A(C_p) eigenvalues are 2cos(2pi k/p) in (-2,2]; the bottom -2 is reached IFF p even
    (k=p/2 exists) = C_p bipartite. p ODD => lambda_min(A) = -2cos(pi/p) > -2 => 2I+A > 0.
    p=7: lambda_min(2I+A(C_7)) = 2-2cos(pi/7) = 4sin^2(pi/14) = 0.19806 = 4cos^2(3pi/7) (HYP-3590, THM-590).

[2] THE WORST MODE (least eigenvector) -- the binding resonance direction:
    p=5: A(C_p) min eigenvalue at Fourier mode k=3 (= (p-1)/2 or (p+1)/2, the near-pi/2 frequency); eigenvector v_j = cos(2pi*3*j/p).
    p=7: A(C_p) min eigenvalue at Fourier mode k=4 (= (p-1)/2 or (p+1)/2, the near-pi/2 frequency); eigenvector v_j = cos(2pi*4*j/p).
    p=11: A(C_p) min eigenvalue at Fourier mode k=6 (= (p-1)/2 or (p+1)/2, the near-pi/2 frequency); eigenvector v_j = cos(2pi*6*j/p).
    => the floor binds in the MIDDLE Fourier mode (k ~ p/2) -- the most-oscillatory resonance,
    which for ODD p never hits the -1 phase exactly (that is the non-bipartiteness).

[3] UNIFORM over all 127 non-full Z_7 cores -- the least-eigenvalue minorant (THM-590):
    gap values over cores: [0.19806, 0.30798, 1.0, 2.0]; the GLOBAL least nonzero-mode eigenvalue = 0.19806
    = 4cos^2(3pi/7) at the doublets. So inf over the finite family of the least eigenvalue is the
    DOUBLET's 4sin^2(pi/14) -- a single set-INDEPENDENT positive number (depends only on p=7).

[4] SET-INDEPENDENCE -- the certificate depends ONLY on the apex prime p:
     apex p  floor = 4sin^2(pi/2p)  = 2-2cos(pi/p)
          3                1.00000         1.00000
          5                0.38197         0.38197
          7                0.19806         0.19806
         11                0.08101         0.08101
         13                0.05812         0.05812
    The covering set never enters; only p does. This is the set-independent floor the gatekeeper
    needs -- a least-eigenvalue (Bochner/SOS) certificate, NOT a per-set estimate.

====================================================================================
CERTIFICATE (clean form): for the apex prime p (odd), the doublet Gram 2I+A(C_p) is positive
definite with lambda_min = 4sin^2(pi/2p) > 0, BECAUSE C_p is non-bipartite (p odd). Over all
non-full Z_p cores the least nonzero-mode eigenvalue is >= this (THM-590). It is set-independent
(only p), and it certifies the sigma-ODD / Bochner / DISCRETE content (the odd cycle is present &
non-degenerate = EXISTENCE, klein-S18), NOT the measure (which binds at the cusp). The floor's
positivity IS the apex cycle's odd length.
====================================================================================
